        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Sync wrapper breaks async views decorated with non_atomic_requests",
        "explanation": "The wrapper is a plain sync function. For an async view, functools.wraps does not make it a coroutine function, so the handler treats it as sync. Under ASGI it is run via sync_to_async and returns an unawaited coroutine, which causes errors. Under WSGI the coroutine check also changes. Previously the original async view was returned unchanged, so this is a regression.",
        "suggestion": "Create an async wrapper when the view is a coroutine function (use iscoroutinefunction), e.g. `async def wrapper(*a, **kw): return await view(*a, **kw)`. Otherwise copy the function instead of wrapping it.",
        "evidence": "    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n        return view(*args, **kwargs)",
        "confidence": 0.7,
